  <office:master-styles><style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/></office:master-styles>
  <office:body><office:text><text:p text:style-name="Title">Field Manual for the Harbour Survey</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Preparation of the survey</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer estimated the routes taken by the ferry during storms before the season ended. The survey team estimated the songs sung at the autumn market while the tide was low. Every visiting student questioned the weight of the fishing nets after each trip with remarkable patience. Every visiting student recorded the songs sung at the autumn market before the season ended.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Boats and routes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The Brindlemoor committee questioned the height of the hedges along the canal with remarkable patience. Every visiting student catalogued the height of the hedges along the canal with remarkable patience. The fictional cooperative described the songs sung at the autumn market using only paper notebooks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Weather and volunteers</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The archive keeper questioned the height of the hedges along the canal despite the persistent fog. Each volunteer questioned the songs sung at the autumn market over three consecutive weeks. The night shift mapped the tidal patterns of the northern bay over three consecutive weeks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Detailed procedure</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The Brindlemoor committee estimated the songs sung at the autumn market according to the old manual. The harbour office measured the tidal patterns of the northern bay before the season ended. The night shift reviewed the condition of the wooden pier while the tide was low.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Common mistakes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew questioned the condition of the wooden pier over three consecutive weeks. The Brindlemoor committee compared the weight of the fishing nets after each trip while the tide was low.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Equipment of the survey</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer estimated the number of lanterns repaired each winter according to the old manual. The night shift described the tidal patterns of the northern bay without any modern instruments. The harbour office measured the growth of moss on the old stone walls with remarkable patience. The survey team compared the condition of the wooden pier using only paper notebooks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Tides and notebooks</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The night shift measured the height of the hedges along the canal according to the old manual. A small working group reviewed the height of the hedges along the canal according to the old manual. The lighthouse crew compared the height of the hedges along the canal according to the old manual.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Lanterns and schedules</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer mapped the songs sung at the autumn market with remarkable patience. The night shift described the weight of the fishing nets after each trip before the season ended. The survey team measured the height of the hedges along the canal over three consecutive weeks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Detailed procedure</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Every visiting student measured the colours of the evening sky over the dunes before the season ended. The survey team estimated the tidal patterns of the northern bay while the tide was low. The night shift catalogued the routes taken by the ferry during storms with remarkable patience.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Common mistakes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew measured the weight of the fishing nets after each trip with remarkable patience. The Brindlemoor committee described the colours of the evening sky over the dunes while the tide was low.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Reporting of the survey</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The harbour office described the songs sung at the autumn market despite the persistent fog. Every visiting student estimated the tidal patterns of the northern bay before the season ended. A small working group measured the colours of the evening sky over the dunes using only paper notebooks. The survey team described the colours of the evening sky over the dunes in a careful and orderly way.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Weather and routes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew described the height of the hedges along the canal without any modern instruments. The harbour office estimated the colours of the evening sky over the dunes with remarkable patience. A small working group recorded the tidal patterns of the northern bay over three consecutive weeks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Records and volunteers</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A small working group questioned the tidal patterns of the northern bay with remarkable patience. The fictional cooperative described the height of the hedges along the canal before the season ended. A small working group questioned the routes taken by the ferry during storms despite the persistent fog.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Detailed procedure</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew recorded the growth of moss on the old stone walls despite the persistent fog. Each volunteer compared the growth of moss on the old stone walls before the season ended. A small working group catalogued the tidal patterns of the northern bay over three consecutive weeks.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_3" text:outline-level="3">Common mistakes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A small working group catalogued the growth of moss on the old stone walls before the season ended. The harbour office summarised the amount of rain collected in copper gauges without any modern instruments.</text:p></office:text></office:body>
</office:document>
